  "interpretation": [
    "The separate data-to-notice native transaction is removed in source. The combined commit still requires multiple file and directory barriers.",
    "Observed queued sequence changes through notice drain fall 1131 to 740 for 384 HTTP requests per source; this includes other queued work and is not exactly384 attributed feed commits.",
    "Observed data-file barrier calls fall 24.75% and directory calls fall 27.67%; absolute time sums are noisy and process-wide.",
    "Five pooled throughput cases rise 1.09% to 37.08%; HashRange batch128 falls 13.36%. This is shared-host evidence, not an isolated causal effect.",
    "The unchanged baseline rate falls from 16.23 to 9.03 writes/sec across its two runs. The candidate also falls 15.02 to 10.07. Host/time variation exceeds the small overall pooled gain.",
    "Every intersecting sampled interval reports substantial foreign I/O; no quiet or maximum-throughput claim is accepted.",
    "Device means are approximate full-interval iostat rates weighted by the clipped time intersection. They include the benchmark and other processes; overlapping device views are not summed.",
    "Foreign bytes retain complete intersecting sample intervals. Their rate denominator is the sum of those full intervals, not exact write time.",
    "comparison.json host reason counts currently count PID-specific reason occurrences. This review instead counts distinct intervals per reason category.",
    "Normal reopen confirms the ordinary product checks only; it does not establish crash, power-loss, cloud, or M5 performance."
  ],
